  "body": "## What changed\n\nRound a part (2D Offset \"Pass starts at\" Inside, Outside, and Auto when it resolves), the rings stay at depth and the links stay in the cut plane. A lift occurs only when each in-plane link fails, and a `link:` note names the reason.\n\n- `level_order::linkable` (the join law of the plan) accepts a chord through air as well as through cut material. A centre is in air when it is 0.1 tool radii or more outside the stock footprint.\n- When the straight chord fails, the plan tries an edge route (`ring_links::edge_route`). The route goes to the edge of the cutter-centre area, along that edge, and back to the next piece. Each chord of the route obeys the same join law. The route goes through each walk vertex on the edge, so a piece that ends there is touched at a shared vertex and not crossed.\n- `ladder_links::pass_link` of a ring area uses the ring law (`ring_links::link`) for all pass link values. The straight link is fed when it is proved. Else the tool lifts to the retract plane, and the tally names the reason: the stay-down limit, the part, a fixture (\"Do not touch\"), a crossing, or uncut stock.\n- A pocket (`around_part: false`) keeps its links byte for byte (#3752 owns it). The entry, the level link and the re-entry after a lift do not change (#3746 owns the entry).\n- No `Links::RINGS` seed: the law is in the motion layer, so an old project file gets the same path. #3750 owns the seed. See `docs/decisions/3747-in-plane-ring-links.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n`pass_start_levels::ring_links`: 80 x 50 stock box, D8, stepover 2, one level.\n\n| Case | Before (lifts, no reason) | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Disc, Inside | 20 | 0 |\n| Disc, Outside / Auto | - | 0 |\n| Dog bone, Inside | 15 | 0 |\n| Dog bone, Outside | - | 0 |\n| Clamp across the band, Inside / Outside | - | 3 / 26, each named (\"fixture\") |\n\nfig8 (heavy, release): Inside 6 lifts in a level, 6 named. Outside 12 lifts, 12 named. Each lift that is left has a named reason.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` `pass_start_levels`: `ring_links::start_side_rings_do_not_lift`, `ring_links::dogbone_start_side_lifts`, `ring_links::lift_reason_is_named` (red first: 20 and 15 lifts, 0 named). The pins also assert no overcut (shape mask, the gouge check) and no crossing feeds (`verify::crossed_pairs`). The clamp pin asserts `avoid_hits` is empty.\n- `camcraft-app` `offset_pass_start`: `lifts::fig8_start_sides_lift_only_with_a_named_reason` (heavy).\n\n## Gates\n\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6): 171 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Targeted heavy step `app heavy: offset_pass_start` (release, `--ignored`): 5 passed, 0 failed. This includes `fig8_start_sides_have_no_crossing`, `fig8_outside_offset_cuts_no_move_at_full_width` and the new pin.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No full heavy lanes and no light lane.\n- The private model of #3741 was not run.\n- 2D Pocket Inside and Outside do not change (#3752).\n- `levels.rs` grows from 457 to 460 lines (one field), and `offset_pass_start.rs` from 418 to 419 lines (one `mod` line). The new code is in `ring_links.rs` (322 lines).\n\n#3423 (lifts between pieces) is covered by this change. Close it when this PR merges.\n\nChangelog: 2D Offset \"Pass starts at\" Inside, Outside and Auto: the rings stay at depth and link in the cut plane (through air or cut material, and along the edge of the area); the tool lifts only where each in-plane link would cut the part, hit a fixture or cross a cut, and a note names the reason.\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #3747\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
